  "configuration_id": "config_008",
  "reason": "Evidence: RNA-only models dominate (0.485–0.650) over image-only (0.208). Within RNA, the encoder choice is the largest source of variation: scvi_n200 (0.650) clearly beats pca_n2000 (0.591) under the same multiprofile+avgpool setting, and avgpool consistently outperforms transformer. The current best is config_005 (scvi_n200, multiprofile, avgpool, 0.650). Question: Does the third available encoder, scgpt, outperform scvi_n200 under the same multiprofile+avgpool conditions? This is a clean single-variable comparison that isolates the encoder effect. Why this experiment: Before investing in multimodal or more complex fusion experiments, it is critical to identify the best RNA encoder so that any multimodal test uses the strongest unimodal baseline. config_008 directly answers whether scgpt is a better or worse representation than scvi_n200, reducing uncertainty about the most impactful design choice (encoder) with minimal confounds, making it the highest-information-per-experiment choice under the limited budget."
}

